<title>DUBAI: Iran oil official says firm oil prices temporary.</title>
<headline>Iran oil official says firm oil prices temporary.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Iranian oil official said on Sunday OPEC members should not bank on a recent hike in oil prices as a lasting trend, the official Iranian news agency IRNA reported.</p>
<p>&quot;The recent hike in oil prices in the international market should not be regarded as a lasting trend,&quot; Mohammad Ali Pourjeddi, head of the OPEC affairs and international relations department at Iran's oil ministry, told the agency.</p>
<p>He said that Iran and other OPEC members &quot;should take the oil prices of the past three or four years as the basis for assessment of their national budget.&quot;</p>
<p>Oil prices recently hit six-year highs.</p>
</text>
